## 0. This file is metered

It is loaded into model prompts - by agent sessions, by hosted review tools that
read instruction files, and by any in-repository tooling that builds prompts
from disk. Each of those has a hard limit, and crossing it does not degrade the
consumer, it **fails** it, on whatever change happens to be in flight.

So this file carries a declared budget and a measured headroom, registered in
[`BUDGETED_DOCS.md`](BUDGETED_DOCS.md).

- **Budget:** <LIMIT_WITH_UNITS>, consumer <WHICH_TOOL_OR_SESSION>.
- **Measure with:** `<BUDGET_CHECK_COMMAND>`.
- **If you extend this file, measure it in the same change** and record the
  number. Growth here arrives from several units at once, each adding a
  paragraph, none of them large.
- Reference material that agents look up rather than read belongs in its own
  file with a link from here. Carving out beats trimming prose.

