## 6. Before you push

The full gate is [`SHIP_CHECKLIST.md`](SHIP_CHECKLIST.md); testing requirements
are [`docs/TESTING_STANDARDS.md`](docs/TESTING_STANDARDS.md). This is the short
list for a routine change:

- [ ] Read the diff as a reviewer would, whole files rather than hunks - a
      windowed view invents defects at its own edges.
- [ ] Section 3 walked: nothing reports a state it did not establish.
- [ ] Section 4 walked: sibling sweep done, every new test mutation-checked.
- [ ] Nothing outside the declared file surface changed.
- [ ] Derived and generated files regenerated by their tool, never hand-edited.
- [ ] Tests meet [`docs/TESTING_STANDARDS.md`](docs/TESTING_STANDARDS.md).
- [ ] **Gates ran last**, after the final edit: `<LINT_COMMAND>`,
      `<TYPECHECK_COMMAND>`, `<TEST_COMMAND>`.
- [ ] If this file or another budget-counted document grew, its budget was
      measured and the number recorded (section 0).
- [ ] You ran it. In this session. Not "should pass".
